(version 1)

# The five gold fingers (X2) are an edge connector: a Nunchuck plug slides over the tongue, so the fingers have to
# run to its tip. They are exactly where the maker drew them: the two front ones 0.14 mm and the three back ones 0.19 mm
# from the tip of the tongue, 0.47 mm or more from its sides. Everything else on the board keeps the normal 0.25 mm from the edge.
(rule "Plug fingers run to the tip of the tongue"
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && A.Reference == 'X2'")
  (constraint edge_clearance (min 0.1mm)))
